content.problemStatement:
Implement the following function:
float Average(char str[], int len);
float Average(char str[], int len);
static float Average(String str){}
static float Average(string str){}
def Average(str):
The function accepts a string 'str' of length 'len' as its argument. Implement the function to
calculate the word average and return the same.
Word Average is calculated by finding the average of the ASCII values of all of the letters in a
word.
Note:
'str' is not null
Input string will contain only lower case English alphabets
The ASCII value of lower case 'a' is 97 while that of 'z' is 122
Do not round off your result, it will be automatically rounded off up to 2 decimal places and
then displayed

code.C:
#include <stdio.h>
int main() {
    int n; char s[2000]; if (scanf("%d %s", &n, s) != 2) return 0;
    double sum = 0;
    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) sum += (unsigned char)s[i];
    printf("%.2f\n", sum / n);
    return 0;
}

code.C++:
#include <iostream>
#include <string>
#include <iomanip>
using namespace std;
int main() {
    int n; string s; if (cin >> n >> s) {
        double sum = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) sum += (unsigned char)s[i];
        cout << fixed << setprecision(2) << (sum / n) << "\n";
    }
    return 0;
}

code.Java:
import java.util.Scanner;
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        if (sc.hasNextInt()) {
            int n = sc.nextInt(); String s = sc.next();
            double sum = 0;
            for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) sum += s.charAt(i);
            System.out.printf("%.2f\n", sum / n);
        }
    }
}

code.Python3:
import sys
def main():
    toks = sys.stdin.read().split()
    if len(toks) >= 2:
        n = int(toks[0])
        s = toks[1]
        avg = sum(ord(c) for c in s[:n]) / n
        print(f"{avg:.2f}")
if __name__ == "__main__": main()

